# inter completion frontier — the crash-fix chunk's before/after
#
# THREE scans of the same 64-cell grid exist for 2026-09-02 and they are NOT
# three measurements of the same tree. Read this before quoting any of them.
#
#   inter_completion_2026-09-02.tsv   24 OK /  6 REFUSED / 34 CRASH
#     The FIRST scan. Its `port=` line names /Users/lilith/tmp/perf1-bin/
#     identity_run.nosym, built 2026-09-02 13:15 local — THREE MINUTES BEFORE
#     commit 628a19cda ("the MD motion search read PAST the source plane")
#     landed at 13:18. So 20 of its 34 crashes are the source-gather panic that
#     commit had already fixed, and the scan describes a tree that was never on
#     main. Kept as the record of that binary; do NOT quote it as a main-branch
#     frontier. The tell is in the numbers: its panic text reads "the len is
#     10816 but the index is 10816", and 10816 = 104*104, i.e. an UNPADDED
#     plane — which is exactly the field 628a19cda changed.
#
#   inter_completion_2026-09-02a.tsv  38 OK /  8 REFUSED / 18 CRASH
#     Same grid re-measured on main at fed59574 (the tip when this chunk
#     started), with a binary built from it. This is the real BEFORE.
#
#   inter_completion_2026-09-02b.tsv  52 OK / 12 REFUSED /  0 CRASH
#     AFTER the two crash fixes below, on main at 4ae1ffb6.
#
# WHAT THE TWO FIXES WERE
#   * `video pic_pd0_lvl 7 …` (4 cells: 568/576/1024/2048 square at p10, and
#     p9 by the same ladder row) — a KEY-frame panic, frame 0 never reached
#     disk. `part_arm::video_pd0_params` skipped `pd0_detector` on an I_SLICE,
#     and the one branch of that function gated ON `slice_type == I_SLICE` is
#     the demote out of PD0_LVL_6. Fixed in commit 4974a859. All four key
#     frames are now byte-IDENTICAL to C.
#   * `leaf must be tested (min_sq <= size <= max_sq)` (14 cells: every size
#     congruent to 40 mod 64 at p8/p10/p13) — an INTER-frame panic.
#     `Pd0Ctx::pick_q` treated "no d1 shape to cost" as "must SPLIT" and
#     descended below `min_sq`, which only an inter frame's
#     `depth_removal_ctrls` can raise above 8. Fixed in commit 4ae1ffb6.
#
# PARTIAL-SB CELLS (the 9 sizes that are not multiples of 64, x 4 presets = 36)
#   first scan : 31 CRASH        (of a binary that predated a landed fix)
#   ...a.tsv   : 15 CRASH, 19 OK,  2 REFUSED
#   ...b.tsv   :  0 CRASH, 33 OK,  3 REFUSED
#
# THE 12 REFUSALS in ...b.tsv are 568/576/1024/2048 square at p6/p8/p10, all of
# them the SAME pre-existing frame-1 refusal ("an inter frame header field is
# not implemented for this configuration"), all of them with frame 0 written
# and byte-identical to C. The count rose from 8 to 12 because the four p10
# cells used to CRASH on the KEY frame and now reach that refusal — no refusal
# was widened to make this scan look green.
#
# IDENT is Y on 5 cells (64/128 at p6; 64/128/256 at p8). That is the byte
# frontier, not the completion one, and it moved for reasons outside this
# chunk (f5804e454).
#
# CONTENT INDEPENDENCE, measured 2026-09-02 so the gradient-only gate is not
# taken on faith: all FIVE content classes the harness has — gradient, screen,
# screenrep, uniform, diag — give the SAME 52 OK / 12 REFUSED / 0 CRASH on this
# grid. The completion frontier is geometry-driven (SB remainder mod 64, and
# the 360p/480p resolution class), not content-driven. `...b-screen.tsv` is the
# screen run, kept because `gradient` never arms the screen-content detector
# and so codes no palette or IntraBC candidate in any cell — the blind spot
# that let two out-of-bounds panics past the STILL panic gate until 2026-08-03.
# The CI gate runs gradient AND screen for that reason, not because they differ
# today.
#
# CROSS-ISA: the AFTER numbers were re-measured on r7900x (x86-64, Linux, 24
# cores) from main at f321cb04 and are IDENTICAL — 64 cells, 52 OK, 12 REFUSED,
# 0 CRASH. Also there: workspace suite 2480/2480, regression spot-check 76/76,
# inter_byte_gate 55 required / 0 failed. On mac the same commit gives 2470
# tests (the count is SIMD-tier dependent), spot-check 76/76, byte gate 55/0,
# identity_full_8bit 1100/1100 and video_key_matrix 58/60.
#
# TIER-2 EVIDENCE for the PD0_LVL_6 fix, taken on the Linux host because
# `-Wl,--wrap` works there: C's own `SVT_PD0CFG_OUT` dump for
# `gradient 568x568 q32 p10` reports `lvl=5` on ALL 81 superblocks of frame 0
# (`islice=1`) and all 81 of frame 1. That is `PD0_LVL_6` demoted to
# `PD0_LVL_5` by `pd0_detector`'s I_SLICE branch — the resolved level the port
# now computes — joined against C's actual ModeDecisionContext rather than
# inferred from the output. The port's frame 0 for that cell is byte-identical
# to C's on both hosts.
#
# host=mac (aarch64, Apple), oracle = reference/svt-av1 on fix/suspected-c-bug-17
# via Bin/Release/libSvtAv1Enc.a. NOTE: `-Wl,--wrap` is rejected by Apple ld64,
# so capture_c_trace builds its BYTE-ONLY variant here and no SVT_* interposer
# can fire on this host — the C-side dumps in docs/ were taken on Linux.
